+A full-control guest can request saved-session metadata only when the host has
+`OMP_COLLAB_HISTORY_KEY_FILE` set to an absolute path and the guest supplies the
+separate history key. A control link alone is not sufficient. View-only links
+cannot use this request.
+
+The key file must contain exactly 32 raw bytes, belong to the host user and
+have no group or other permissions. The host refuses symlinks. Set the variable
+before starting omp. Without it, saved-session access is disabled.
+
+The guest sends the key as unpadded base64url in the encrypted Collab request.
+Keep the key separate from Collab links. The host reads the file for each request,
+so replacing or removing it changes access for the next request.
 
 The list uses offset pagination and can change between requests if sessions
 change. This request does not provide saved message history.
